= Shortcut learning — Simple =

'''Shortcut learning''' happens when a model finds an easy clue that works on the training data but is not the robust pattern we wanted it to learn.

For example, an image model might classify an animal partly from the background instead of the animal itself.

The shortcut can work very well on a benchmark.

It becomes a problem when the clue changes or disappears in real use.

Shortcut learning often uses spurious correlations, but the two terms are not exactly the same.

